.TH QPP 1 "September 2026" "Qore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qpp \- generate C++ bindings and documentation from Qore QPP definitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qpp
.RI [ options ] " input-files..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qpp
processes QPP definitions used by the Qore runtime and native modules.
It can generate C++ source, API documentation, metadata, and compile-time stubs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o , " \-\-output=" file
Write generated C++ source to the given file.
.TP
.BR \-d , " \-\-dox-output=" file
Write Doxygen documentation to the given file.
.TP
.BR \-m , " \-\-metadata=" file
Write JSON API metadata to the given file.
.TP
.BR \-\-file-prefix-map= OLD=NEW
Replace a source filename prefix in JSON metadata, builtin reflection locations
and generated stub comments. May be repeated; the last matching prefix wins.
Input files and C++ line directives keep their original paths, allowing the
native compiler to apply its own debug-prefix maps. CMake builds automatically
forward the compiler's file-prefix maps to qpp.
.TP
.BR \-s , " \-\-stub-output=" file
Write a Qore compile-time stub to the given file.
.TP
.BR \-D , " \-\-define=" name
Define a preprocessor macro. May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show all available options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B qpp
reports problems on standard error as errors or warnings.  An error means that
an output would be wrong or incomplete, for example a function with functional
domains or code flags but no long comment, whose documentation would lack the
restriction or code flag note.  After it has reported every error in its input,
.B qpp
exits with status 1 if it reported any error and removes the output files that
it wrote in that run, so that the build fails and the next build runs it again.
A problem that leaves the output complete is reported as a warning and does not
change the exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qore (1),
.BR qcc (1),
.BR qdx (1)
